REVIEW-BRAIN PROVENANCE — proposal patch for the agent-team chain's own merger.
Lead-owned files: a seat may ONLY read and cite them, never edit them (chain law
11), so this file is the handover and the fix travels as hunks.

TARGET: .github/scripts/turn_segment.sh   (the review-output extractor, :548-574)
TARGET: .github/workflows/agent-team.yml  (the turn job outputs :313-316 and the
        "SEGREGATION bookkeeping" step that writes agent-team/REVIEW-LOG.org)
STATUS: PROPOSAL — NOT APPLIED. Both targets are Lead-owned.
APPLY:  git apply --check docs/review-provenance-fix.patch
        git apply       docs/review-provenance-fix.patch
ROT-PROOF: python3 scripts/chain_patch_check.py grades THAT this patch still
        applies to the files it names. Its handover roster and pin now count
        THREE patches — that literal moved in the same commit as this patch, per
        the POPULATION leg's own rule ("a new handover must be added here in the
        same commit that writes it, or the check refuses rather than grading less
        than it claims").
WHAT IS BROKEN — measured, not replayed from a Lead note:

  The chain has taken FIVE verdicts in a row from a provider-SUBSTITUTED reviewer
  brain while the record read as the duty reviewer's own work. Evidence quoted in
  TEAM-CONTROL.org:8 (Lead cycles 10-az, 10-bc, 10-bf, 10-bh, 10-bj — "qfmodel
  substitution 3RD/4TH/5TH CONSECUTIVE EPISODE", transcripts review-transcript-420
  / -421 / -422 / -425, first line each: "Model deepseek-v4.1-flash is not
  available right now; using qfmodel instead"). Lead 10-bh scheduled the fix:
  "automated provenance stamping (grep transcript line 1 for the substitution
  pattern, stamp the ci-review record) scheduled for the next machinery pass".

  Why the existing plumbing cannot see it: .github/scripts/turn_segment.sh:561
  conditions the marker grep on `[ -z "$REVIEW_VERDICT" ]`, so the substitution
  string is only consulted when NO verdict parsed. A substituted reviewer that
  still prints `VERDICT:` therefore answers lane_dead=0 (:574) and the merger
  writes a REVIEW-LOG record naming the DUTY reviewer as the brain — the record
  group at agent-team.yml:1056-1066 emits only AUTHOR / REVIEWER / VERDICT /
  OUTCOME / WHEN, so nothing in the durable audit trail says which brain judged.

WHAT THIS PATCH DOES:

  1. turn_segment.sh computes the substitution stamp UNCONDITIONALLY (whenever a
     branch was pending), capturing the substitute's own name from its marker
     line, whitelisted to [A-Za-z0-9._:@-] and length-capped, and exports
     review_substituted / review_sub_brain as step outputs next to the existing
     review_lane_dead. lane_dead keeps its own condition and value: the patch
     does not reclassify anything.
  2. agent-team.yml maps the two new outputs into the job outputs (beside
     review_lane_dead, :316) and passes them into the bookkeeping step as an
     `env:` mapping — NOT inline `${{ }}` interpolation: the value is a fragment
     of the reviewer CLI's stdout, so it must never be written into the script
     text that bash executes.
  3. The REVIEW-LOG record gains `:SUBSTITUTED: no` or `:SUBSTITUTED: yes
     (<brain> substituted)` between VERDICT and OUTCOME, and the record body
     names the same fact. It is provenance ONLY: OUTCOME, NEWPENDING, the verdict
     roster and the stall law are untouched, so a produced verdict stays a
     verdict — exactly the Lead's ruling in 10-az ("NOT counted a review-miss (a
     verdict was produced)").

WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT CHANGE:

  * No outcome, no park/retain rule, no merge decision. The record of a verdict
    judged by a substitute is still an APPROVED/REJECTED verdict; the stamp makes
    the substitution visible so the Lead's audit can weigh it, which is the class
    of false trust 10-az recorded when a substitute also violated the read-only
    brief and committed inside the container (e47baab).
  * The existing honest-lane guard (lead cycle 10-l, job 120814481260) is kept
    verbatim; the new block sits after its `fi` and reuses its marker string, so
    the two can never disagree about what a substitution is.

MEASURED on this tree before shipping (nothing here is asserted from prose):

  * `git apply --check` CLEAN against the untouched carriers, and the hunks apply
    and re-apply on a clean checkout; after applying: `bash -n` clean on
    turn_segment.sh and the workflow parses as YAML.
  * Functional controls over the EXTRACTED block (the shipped text, run against
    fabricated review outputs, never against the repo):
      A substituted + `VERDICT: APPROVED` (the 5-episode class) -> review_verdict
        =APPROVED, lane_dead=0, substituted=1, sub_brain=qfmodel;
      B honest duty reviewer -> substituted=0, sub_brain empty;
      C substituted + NO verdict -> lane_dead=1 AND substituted=1 (the old guard
        still fires — no regression);
      D reviewer stdout carrying `$(touch …)` / backticks in the brain slot -> no
        file created, exported value carries no shell metacharacter;
      E no pending branch -> substituted=0 (no stamp without a review).
  * Functional controls over the EXTRACTED record block: `:SUBSTITUTED:` renders
    for substituted / honest / output-absent (an older turn job writes no value,
    so the record says `no`, never a guess) and a hostile env value is inert.
  * Carrier graders, patched vs base: `scripts/chain_slot_check.py` 4/4 GREEN on
    BOTH (rc 0); `scripts/chain_session_check.py` output BYTE-IDENTICAL patched
    vs base (still the known 12 Lead-owned problems — this patch does not claim
    to touch the session loop; docs/session-loop-fix.patch owns that).
  * `python3 scripts/chain_patch_check.py` -> rc 0 counting 3 handovers;
    `--selftest` -> rc 0, 12/12 controls (the extra-handover control's needle is
    decoupled from the count, so a roster bump can never false-red it).

RISK NOTE: the marker string is the qoder CLI's own wording ("is not available
right now; using … instead"), the same one 10-l already depends on. A harness
that rewords it silently degrades to `:SUBSTITUTED: no` — a lost stamp, never a
false accusation. If the Lead wants the stamp to GRADE anything (refuse an
APPROVED verdict from a substituted brain, or escalate after N substitutions),
that is a separate law decision: it changes outcomes and belongs in
chain_slot_check's verdict roster, not in this handover.

ON LANDING: relabel this file `STATUS: RETIRED` and DELETE it from docs/ in the
same commit that bumps HANDOVERS/EXPECTED_PATCHES in
scripts/chain_patch_check.py — the POPULATION leg refuses a roster that does not
match docs/ on disk, so a retired-but-kept handover must still be graded by a
harness that exits 0, and nothing today grades the `:SUBSTITUTED:` record line.
Naming a grader that does not exist is the shape this patch family exists to
refuse (see docs/pending-slot-fix.patch, retired against chain_slot_check.py
because that harness really does measure the landed guard).

